From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:51:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e001de-devkit: Mark the EC reset gpio as
 reserved
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.65
Git-commit: 0297c8e98a054fc2a0afcb96114f57603a02594e

[ Upstream commit 0297c8e98a054fc2a0afcb96114f57603a02594e ]

GPIO 65 from TLMM is used by the embedded controller as its reset line.

On some devices, toggling the embedded controller reset line makes the
device not power up at all, unless the battery is unplugged.

So reserve it in order to prevent Linux from requesting or
reconfiguring it.

Fixes: 7b8a31e82b87 ("arm64: dts: qcom: Add X1E001DE Snapdragon Devkit for Windows")
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260922-dts-qcom-hamoa-reserve-ec-reset-gpio-v3-2-fde7f8a53382@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <bjorn.andersson@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e001de-devkit.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e001de-devkit.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e001de-devkit.dts
index 701f35af7d5c..bc15a988f301 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e001de-devkit.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e001de-devkit.dts
@@ -1188,7 +1188,8 @@ wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 };
 
 &tlmm {
-	gpio-reserved-ranges = <44 4>; /* SPI (TPM) */
+	gpio-reserved-ranges = <44 4>, /* SPI (TPM) */
+			       <65 1>; /* EC reset */
 
 	eusb3_reset_n: eusb3-reset-n-state {
 		pins = "gpio6";
-- 
2.56.0

